  "format": {
    "summary": "Authored stage 2 tower (floors 13-17, 3120 px wide). Same shape the stage 3 generator will output, so the loader and renderer written now keep working; only the source changes (this file now, a saved generated layout later). Instances of templates.json templates; numbers from balance.world / balance.generator.",
    "floor": "{number, purpose, difficulty (1-10), expectedMinutes, stairwell, scriptedSpawns?, left, right}. left = west wing (x 0-1440), right = east wing (x 1680-3120).",
    "stairwell": "{xMin 1440, xMax 1680, landing:{xMin,xMax,stairsX}}. The stairs/shaft are in the middle (stairsX 1560). Each wing's front door is at its stairwell edge: x 1440 (left) and x 1680 (right). The landing is not part of any unit.",
    "unit": "{id (f<floor><L|R>), template (templates.json id), condition (normal|ransacked|burned), name, flavour, frontDoor (open|jammed), rooms[], objects[], zombies[], survivors[], questItems[]}.",
    "room": "{ref, type (templates.json roomTypes), modules, startModule (0 = at the front door, 5 = far end), doorAfter (open|jammed|none)}. Array order is the room index used in ids, laid out from the front door outward. doorAfter is the interior door on the room's FAR boundary at d = (startModule + modules) * 240; it is not a slot object and never blocks walking. Room x span: left wing x = 1440 - d, right wing x = 1680 + d.",
    "slotFormula": "Room of N modules has floor0..floor(2N-1) and wall0..wall(2N-1), numbered outward from the room's front-door side. For slot k: d = startModule*240 + 240*floor(k/2) + (k even ? 72 : 168); left x = 1440 - d, right x = 1680 + d. Equivalent lookup by absolute index a = 2*startModule + k: left x = [1368,1272,1128,1032,888,792,648,552,408,312,168,72][a], right x = [1752,1848,1992,2088,2232,2328,2472,2568,2712,2808,2952,3048][a]. Same-layer pairs are >= 96 px apart; every slot is >= 72 px from a doorway. The outermost slots sit 72 px from the world edge (x 72 and 3048) by formula.",
    "object": "{id (f<floor><L|R>-<roomIndex>-<slot>), objectId (balance.objects), room (room ref), slot (floorN|wallN), x, layer (floor|wall), lootTable? (defaults to balance.objects[objectId].primary.lootTable), fixedLoot? [{id,qty}] (first search gives exactly these, 0 table rolls unless rolls), rolls? [min,max], foundNote? {id} (text in templates.json notes[] / floorOverrides / authored), empty? true (ransacked or burned container: searching gives the empty line from loot.json emptyLines; fixedLoot objects are never empty), was? (objectId a burned charred_debris replaced), fixture? true (workbench: Use only), note? (designer comment, ignore at runtime)}.",
    "zombie": "{id, type (crawler|walker), x, facing (left|right), room (ref)}. facing is the world direction the zombie looks. In the left wing 'away from the unit door' = left, in the right wing = right.",
    "survivors": "[{id, x, layer, room}]. questItems: [{id, container (object id)}] pointing at fixedLoot quest goods.",
    "buildSpots": "Optional on a unit (f15L now; stage 3 derives it from empty slots). {barricade:{x}, floor:[{id,room,slot,x,requiresEmptySlot?}], window:[...]}. Floor spots are empty floor slots, window spots empty wall slots; requiresEmptySlot = usable only once the object in that slot is dismantled.",
    "notesCount": "Quest and tutorial notes (note_mara_bag, hint_nails) do not count toward notesPerFloor.",
    "scriptedSpawns": "Floor 15: [{id, type, x, facing, trigger}] spawned on the landing outside the start flat when the trigger fires.",
    "condition": "Marks flavour and loot. ransacked: some objects absent, containers marked empty (drawers open, papers). burned: charred_debris with 'was', broken windows, containers empty. Objects with fixedLoot and the guaranteed toilet tank are exempt.",
    "guaranteesApplied": "Food (fixedLoot canned_food/dry_snack in a kitchen cupboard) on every floor, in a flat. Clean water (water_bottle) on 14 and 16 in a fridge. Drainable toilet tank (uncharred) on every floor. Floor 15 food is in the right flat; the start flat fridge does not count.",
    "zombieRules": "No zombie in module 0 of any unit. At most 1 walker in a unit's first room (none are placed there at all). Walker pairs: same room, both face away from the unit door, both >= 150 px from the unit entrance (d >= 150; here all pairs are d >= 800). Never more than 2 walkers in a room. Most zombies face away from the unit door; a few crawlers face toward it (the generator uses 0.7 away)."
  },
